, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to anchor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to secure a ship in the water with an anchor", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We anchored 25 miles from Lima.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to sit ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be located", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The city sits on the cliffs over the sea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cliff", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a steep rock near the sea", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have to take a bus up the cliffs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "I can't handle \u2026 ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "too much to deal with ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My knees can't handle the walk. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take a break ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take a rest", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can take a break soon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Saying How Far a Place Is", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the prepositions <span class=\"strong\">from </span> and <span class=\"strong\">to </span> when you want to talk about how far a place is. <br><br>  You use <span class=